te\": \"8fd757fce8958108741ed23bc552141087636299\",\n+  \"base\": \"4c22efe839a5a408b46840352943def280412784\",\n+  \"harness\": \"a5ecf975923c1c024ee98adf849016181dd6e482\",\n+  \"files\": [\n+    \"run-empire-v2.js\",\n+    \"CHANGELOG.md\"\n+  ]\n+}\ndiff --git a/ogz-meta/inbox/codex/2026-10-01/stop1-retire-exit-selector/EVIDENCE.md b/ogz-meta/inbox/codex/2026-10-01/stop1-retire-exit-selector/EVIDENCE.md\nnew file mode 100644\nindex 00000000..b2220fa2\n--- /dev/null\n+++ b/ogz-meta/inbox/codex/2026-10-01/stop1-retire-exit-selector/EVIDENCE.md\n@@ -0,0 +1,23 @@\n+# Evidence status\n+\n+Fresh selected-tree behavior is pending. The sibling [REDACTED] packet recorded a passing prepared comparison [REDACTED]: the old constructor boundary throws on absent selector.toUpperCase; the exact retirement proceeds beyond that boundary with no replacement property. This historical preparation does not prove a future staged tree.\n+\n+After root captures the real candidate:\n+\n+    EXIT_SELECTOR_REVIEW_TREE=<actual-tree> node ogz-meta/inbox/codex/2026-10-01/stop1-retire-exit-selector/fixtures/verify.cjs\n+\n+The copied fixture is byte-identical, at the same relative depth. It reads immutable runner/settings blobs, applies no patches in exact-tree mode, extracts actual constructor statements via Acorn, and executes the affected boundary. It records runner hashes and selected tree in verification-TREE.json. Root should preserve the full result in delivery/ after running.\n+\n+Readiness census found the obsolete block as the sole active producer/consumer of [REDACTED]_SYSTEM in runtime sources. Canonical settings has no selector property. Residual test references cover historic mock snapshots, ambient environment preservation or rejected profile keys, not runtime selector production. Reconfirm scoped source when integrating.\n+\n+Limits: constructor-boundary execution is not whole-bot boot, broker/exit execution, deployment or current PM2 health. No exit behavior or profitability claim follows.\n+\n+Prepared packager defaults to review-result.json; explicit additional completed result basenames may be supplied. It preserves full results, scoped ledger rows and raw output with original/redacted/compressed hashes and existing secret redaction. Run validate-tapes.cjs against completed artifacts; no tape validation is claimed in advance.\n+\n+## Exact candidate verification, 2026-10-02\n+\n+Candidate 8fd757fce8958108741ed23bc552141087636299 against base 4c22efe839a5a408b46840352943def280412784. delivery/behavior.json records constructor-boundary PASS with immutable source and no source patches. Existing boundary throws on absent selector; candidate continues without replacement. Fresh tracked runtime JS/JSON census identifies only removed runner references; no other active selector owner.\n+\n+First Mercury launch stopped before provider review because the sibling working configuration no longer matched qualified harness a5ecf975923c1c024ee98adf849016181dd6e482 (missing consensus.emergencyModel). The review launcher now pins that harness tree’s configuration via MERCURY_CONFIG_FILE. Shared Mercury source/configuration was not changed. Full failed launch is preserved in private/review.log and packaged tapes.\n+\n+Astra completed no_break_found after a preserved usage-limit failure and Trey's reset. Final host proof uses actual parent 4c22efe8; prior older-baseline evidence is delivery/behavior-older-baseline.json. Fixture SHA256: f65c7d44a274b3dd26630f22af34886e70eff71159a5450d7282164321878148. No production change between review and final proof.\ndiff --git a/ogz-meta/inbox/codex/2026-10-01/stop1-retire-exit-selector/INHERITED.md b/ogz-meta/inbox/codex/2026-10-01/stop1-retire-exit-selector/INHERITED.md\nnew file mode 100644\nindex 00000000..28af3d6d\n--- /dev/null\n+++ b/ogz-meta/inbox/codex/2026-10-01/stop1-retire-exit-selector/INHERITED.md\n@@ -0,0 +1,5 @@\n+# Inherited boundary\n+\n+Runner contains unrelated uncommitted backtest logging/state-restoration work. This mission neither adopts nor removes those hunks. Historical EXIT_SYSTEM references in archived documents/tests are not active ownership and are not deleted in this lane.\n+\n+The defect is a removed canonical configuration value still dereferenced by a dead constructor log. The fix is deleting that obsolete consumer, not introducing a default, throw, runtime stop or new configuration option. Actual exit modules and policy are untouched. No process restart or broad Stop1 completion is claimed.\ndiff --git a/ogz-meta/inbox/codex/2026-10-01/stop1-retire-exit-selector/MANIFEST.md b/ogz-meta/inbox/codex/2026-10-01/stop1-retire-exit-selector/MANIFEST.md\nnew file mode 100644\nindex 00000000..5d2d87d0\n--- /dev/null\n+++ b/ogz-meta/inbox/codex/2026-10-01/stop1-retire-exit-selector/MANIFEST.md\n@@ -0,0 +1,9 @@\n+# Provenance\n+\n+Date:2026-10-01. Sources: parent task; sibling [REDACTED]/retire.patch and fixtures/verify.cjs; current Stop1 Mercury+Kimi driver and tape packaging. Kept for atomic delivery of six-line obsolete-selector retirement.\n+\n+delivery/fixture-provenance.json records byte-identical copy hashes. Curated preparation: six docs, retire.patch, fixtures/verify.cjs, fixture provenance, run-review.cjs, package-tapes.cjs and validate-tapes.cjs. Root adds real CANDIDATE.json, exact behavior output, review decision and validated tape artifacts.\n+\n+Exclude private/, generated copies and unrelated runner edits. Root owns staging, final source diff, atomic commit and remote confirmation. This packet does not fabricate a candidate or claim a pending review passed.\n+\n+Final fixture differs from its historical copy only by reading baseline from CANDIDATE.json. Final hash is in EVIDENCE.md. Both baseline receipts, both Astra attempts and Mercury failure/recovery tapes are retained. No private raw files staged.\ndiff --git a/ogz-meta/inbox/codex/2026-10-01/stop1-retire-exit-selector/MISSION.md b/ogz-meta/inbox/codex/2026-10-01/stop1-retire-exit-selector/MISSION.md\nnew file mode 100644\nindex 00000000..cfd590f9\n--- /dev/null\n+++ b/ogz-meta/inbox/codex/2026-10-01/stop1-retire-exit-selector/MISSION.md\n@@ -0,0 +1,5 @@\n+# Retire nonexistent exit selector\n+\n+Date:2026-10-01. Dispatcher:Trey through root Codex. Stop1 authorizes configuration ownership cleanup; root delegated packet preparation after RSI2. This single change removes the obsolete six-line runner constructor block that reads nonexistent exits.exitSystem and calls toUpperCase on it. No exit-policy change, replacement selector, feature flag, default or gate is authorized.\n+\n+Root supplies real CANDIDATE.json after RSI2 delivery. No source identity or review verdict is fabricated in this preparation.\ndiff --git a/ogz-meta/inbox/codex/2026-10-01/stop1-retire-exit-selector/REVIEW.md b/ogz-meta/inbox/codex/2026-10-01/stop1-retire-exit-selector/REVIEW.md\nnew file mode 100644\nindex 00000000..4e2df648\n--- /dev/null\n+++ b/ogz-meta/inbox/codex/2026-10-01/stop1-retire-exit-selector/REVIEW.md\n@@ -0,0 +1,11 @@\n+# Exit-selector review closure — 2026-10-02\n+\n+Candidate 8fd757fce8958108741ed23bc552141087636299; base 4c22efe839a5a408b46840352943def280412784. Production change is exactly six removed runner lines, with changelog. Harness source/config pinned together to a5ecf975923c1c024ee98adf849016181dd6e482.\n+\n+Mercury run 2026-10-02T12-08-11-248Z-836827b3dc1d completed in nine iterations: no_break_found, answer_given. It used grep, git_diff, find_references and Serena property references. Provider HTTP 503 recovered through the existing retry. The receipt identifies baseline tree 4b3901650c779d1834f2704ee1e4a407b2662fac, resolved from the base commit.\n+\n+Independent gpt-6-astra review completed no_break_found with provider SSE identity verified. It searched 1,248 tracked source/config/script files and traced unchanged ECM, pattern exits, OrderExecutor, TradingLoop, and PolicyBuilder. Its initial attempt ended with usage-limit error; after Trey reported a reset, the same review was retried. Both full attempts are retained. Fable/Kimi were not invoked: unavailable subscriptions/balance were previously recorded and Trey selected Astra.\n+\n+Astra correctly noted that the host proof originally compared an older baseline. Root changed the fixture to obtain its base from CANDIDATE.json and reran against actual parent 4c22efe8: baseline throws, candidate proceeds. Production bytes were unchanged. Both behavior receipts are retained; the final fixture hash is recorded in EVIDENCE.md. No unresolved source finding remains.\n+\n+Mercury's assertion that searches mean no regression can occur is too broad. Its search is evidence of no named selector references, not every possible dynamic access or runtime behavior. Astra independently traced the retained exit owners. Neither reviewer executed tests; host proof executes only the constructor boundary. No full boot, broker, trade, exit-policy execution, PM2 activation or profitability is claimed.\ndiff --git a/ogz-meta/inbox/codex/2026-10-01/stop1-retire-exit-selector/TAPE-VALIDATION.json b/ogz-meta/inbox/codex/2026-10-01/stop1-retire-exit-selector/TAPE-VALIDATION.json\nnew file mode 100644\nindex 00000000..50d22435\n--- /dev/null\n+++ b/ogz-meta/inbox/codex/2026-10-01/stop1-retire-exit-selector/TAPE-VALIDATION.json\n@@ -0,0 +1,8 @@\n+{\n+  \"result\": \"PASS\",\n+  \"records\": 44,\n+  \"uniquePayloads\": 43,\n+  \"errors\": [],\n+  \"findings\": [],\n+  \"metadataFalsePositives\": []\n+}\ndiff --git a/ogz-meta/inbox/codex/2026-10-01/stop1-retire-exit-selector/TAPES.json b/ogz-meta/inbox/codex/2026-10-01/stop1-retire-exit-selector/TAPES.json\nnew file mode 100644\nindex 00000000..7b93e650\n--- /dev/null\n+++ b/ogz-meta/inbox/codex/2026-10-01/stop1-retire-exit-selector/TAPES.json\n@@ -0,0 +1,504 @@\n+{\n+  \"date\": \"2026-10-01\",\n+  \"scope\": [\n+    \"review-result.json\",\n+    \"astra-result.json\"\n+  ],\n+  \"encoding\": \"Content-addressed gzip of UTF-8 redact